---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Terms & Conditions | Racing Pigeon Testing';
const description = 'Terms for SENO Biotech racing-pigeon testing: orders, sample shipping and retention, turnaround, payment and taxes, reports, refunds, export compliance and liability.';

const hreflang = [
  { lang: 'en', href: 'https://senopigeon.com/en/terms/' },
  { lang: 'zh-CN', href: 'https://senopigeon.com/tiaokuan/' },
  { lang: 'x-default', href: 'https://senopigeon.com/tiaokuan/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en" canonical="/en/terms/" {hreflang}>
  <Header />

  <main id="main">

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-900 to-brand-700 py-16 text-white">
    <div class="container-x">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-brand-100">Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-x py-16">
    <div class="prose prose-gray mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2>1. Definitions and acceptance</h2>
      <p>These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) form an agreement between you (“Customer”, “you”) and Zhangjiakou SENO Biotech Co., Ltd. (“Company”, “we”, “us”) for racing-pigeon gene testing, pathogen testing, DNA ID/kinship testing, diagnostic kits and related services.</p>
      <p>By requesting a quotation, placing an order, paying an invoice, submitting a sample or instructing a distributor, you confirm that you have read and accept these Terms and our Privacy Policy. If you order for a company or other organisation, you confirm that you are authorised to bind it. If you do not agree, do not use the services.</p>

      <h2>2. Eligibility and use restrictions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must have full legal capacity. The services are not directed to minors.</li>
        <li>All services are for racing-pigeon and other avian breeding, health management and research reference. They are not for human medical diagnosis or treatment, food processing or pharmaceutical use.</li>
        <li>Kits are supplied as research-use-only (RUO) unless the order or product label expressly states that a product is a registered in-vitro diagnostic (IVD). You are responsible for confirming registration, import and use requirements in your destination country.</li>
        <li>You must not use results for fraud, pedigree falsification, misleading trade, unlawful breeding or any other unlawful purpose.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Scope of services and order formation</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Services include analysis of eight candidate performance-associated loci (LDHA, DRD4, CRY1, MSTN, F-KER, LRP8, GSR and CASK), a 12-pathogen qPCR panel, DNA ID/kinship testing, related kits and laboratory technical support.</li>
        <li>Prices, turnaround times and test menus on the website are indicative. The final scope, format, price and delivery terms are those in the accepted quotation, invoice or order confirmation.</li>
        <li>We may decline or cancel an order for sample, compliance, capacity or force-majeure reasons. Amounts paid for services not performed will be refunded for the unperformed portion.</li>
        <li>You must provide accurate contact, shipping, billing and sample-list information. Costs caused by incorrect information, re-routing, return, customs clearance or re-shipment are your responsibility.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Prices, taxes and payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Unless a quotation states otherwise, prices are in USD or the quoted currency, ex-works China, and exclude international freight, insurance, duties, VAT, customs fees and other destination taxes.</li>
        <li>Payment methods are those shown on the invoice and may include bank transfer and PayPal. Testing or dispatch begins only after the agreed payment is received. Third-party payment fees, exchange losses and refund fees are borne by the Customer, except where law provides otherwise.</li>
        <li>The Customer is responsible for import duties, VAT, customs-agent fees and other statutory charges. We are not responsible for return, destruction or delay caused by unpaid taxes.</li>
        <li>Invoices and payment records are retained under applicable accounting and tax law. Invoice-detail changes must be requested before invoicing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Sample shipping, receipt and disposal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Customer must collect, package, label and ship samples in accordance with our sampling guide and confirm that samples are avian/racing-pigeon samples matching the order. Use leak-proof, contamination-resistant packaging and comply with carrier and biological-sample rules.</li>
        <li>The Customer is responsible for export, import, quarantine and other permits. Detention, return, destruction or fines caused by missing permits, misdeclaration or carrier-rule breaches are the Customer’s responsibility.</li>
        <li>On arrival we check appearance, quantity and sample IDs. We may reject, request re-sampling or process as received for leaking, putrid, contaminated, poorly labelled or insufficient samples, and will notify the Customer.</li>
        <li>Unless the order, a written agreement or law provides otherwise, samples are retained for 30 days after report delivery for necessary re-testing or dispute handling, then inactivated/disposed of under biosample procedures. The Customer may request earlier disposal in writing, subject to legal retention obligations.</li>
        <li>Samples are biological materials and travel with risks of leakage, delay, temperature excursion or customs detention. The Customer should arrange appropriate transit insurance.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Testing, quality control and reports</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Methods include real-time quantitative PCR (qPCR), STR typing and related molecular techniques. The method, sample type and QC requirements are those stated in the project description and report.</li>
        <li>We follow internal QC procedures with positive/negative controls, internal or amplification controls, and review of anomalous results. If QC fails, we may request a new sample or repeat the test.</li>
        <li>Reports are normally issued as PDF to the nominated email and may include sample ID, test menu, results, interpretation, method, limitations and references. The Customer should check names/ring numbers and keep the report securely.</li>
        <li>Reports depend on the submitted sample and information provided. We do not guarantee sample provenance, label accuracy or the Customer’s downstream use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Turnaround and delays</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Pathogen reports are normally issued 2–3 working days after a sample arrives and passes intake QC. Flight-gene and DNA ID/kinship reports normally take 7–14 working days.</li>
        <li>These periods are estimates and exclude weekends, public holidays, customs inspection, carrier delay, re-sampling, re-testing and force majeure. Peak volume, reagent supply or equipment maintenance may cause delay; we will notify you as soon as practicable.</li>
        <li>Do not make race, sale, breeding or other dependent decisions before receiving the formal report. We are not liable for losses based on the Customer’s own assumptions about timing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="refunds">8. Cancellation, refunds and re-tests</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Before a sample enters testing, the Customer may cancel in writing; refunds are net of payment fees, logistics, consumables and administrative costs already incurred.</li>
        <li>Once extraction, amplification, sequencing or reporting has begun, the service is customised and performed; cancellation and refunds are not available in principle, except where mandatory law provides otherwise.</li>
        <li>If our operational error, QC failure or a clearly incorrect report makes the result unusable, we will prioritise a free re-test; if re-testing is not possible, we will refund the unperformed portion.</li>
        <li>If sample quality, contamination, insufficient quantity, wrong labelling, incorrect Customer information or transit damage prevents testing or affects the result, re-sampling and re-testing are at the Customer’s cost; we may assist with troubleshooting.</li>
        <li>Kits are not returnable without cause because of cold-chain and biological-material constraints. For damaged, wrong or short shipments, notify us within 7 days of delivery with photos, batch number and order number; after verification we will replace or refund.</li>
        <li>Nothing in this section excludes non-waivable consumer rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Interpretation and disclaimers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Gene testing provides candidate-gene association and probabilistic information, not a race prediction, health diagnosis or breeding guarantee. Performance is influenced by multiple genes, training, nutrition, environment, health and chance.</li>
        <li>Pathogen results must be interpreted with clinical signs, epidemiology, sample quality and loft management. A single negative does not exclude infection; a positive does not necessarily mean clinical disease.</li>
        <li>Site content and reports are not veterinary diagnosis or treatment advice. Consult a licensed veterinarian when birds show signs of illness. Results are not advice on human health.</li>
        <li>Scientific understanding, methods and interpretation standards may evolve. An older report does not automatically become invalid, but should be read with its date and the method used at the time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. Intellectual property and confidentiality</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The website, testing workflows, primer/probe designs, report templates, databases and trade marks belong to the Company or relevant rights holders. The Customer may not copy, reverse-engineer, resell or use them for competing services without written permission.</li>
        <li>The Customer receives a right to use the report for its own breeding, trade explanation and internal management. When showing it to third parties, the Customer must avoid disclosing others’ personal or sample information.</li>
        <li>Each party will keep confidential the other’s trade secrets, prices, customer information and technical materials, except where disclosure is required by law.</li>
        <li>We may use de-identified, aggregated testing data for quality control, statistical analysis and method improvement; this does not include identifiable personal or loft information.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Data protection</h2>
      <p>We process personal information, samples and testing data under our Privacy Policy. The Customer must have the necessary authority for personal information it provides and should provide only what is needed for testing. Cross-border transfers are covered by section 6 of the Privacy Policy. The Privacy Policy forms part of these Terms; if the two conflict on data protection, the Privacy Policy prevails.</p>

      <h2>12. Export, sanctions and local compliance</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Customer must comply with import, export, sanctions, biosecurity, animal-quarantine and IVD rules in its jurisdiction and obtain required permits.</li>
        <li>We do not provide services to persons, entities, regions or end uses restricted by applicable sanctions or export controls. We may request end-user/end-use information and may decline or suspend suspicious orders.</li>
        <li>Kits, samples and services must not be used for biological weapons, unlawful modification or other prohibited purposes.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>13. Liability and indemnity</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Company’s total liability for all claims relating to a particular order shall not exceed the amount actually paid by the Customer for that order.</li>
        <li>We are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, including lost profit, prize money, breeder value, goodwill, data or opportunity; liabilities that cannot be excluded by law are excluded from this limitation.</li>
        <li>The limitation does not apply to our wilful misconduct or gross negligence, fraud, personal injury or liabilities that mandatory law does not allow us to limit.</li>
        <li>The Customer will indemnify us and our affiliates against reasonable losses, fines and legal costs arising from the Customer’s breach of these Terms, misuse of products/reports, infringement of third-party rights or breach of import/export or biosecurity law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>14. Force majeure</h2>
      <p>Neither party is liable for delay or failure caused by events beyond its reasonable control, including natural disaster, epidemic, war, government action, customs inspection, carrier interruption, strike, cyber-attack, power or equipment failure. The affected party will notify the other promptly and use reasonable efforts to mitigate. If the event continues beyond a reasonable period, either party may terminate the unperformed portion and settle for services actually performed.</p>

      <h2>15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>These Terms are governed by the laws of the People’s Republic of China, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.</li>
        <li>The parties will first attempt good-faith negotiation. If unresolved, the dispute will be submitted to the competent People’s Court in Zhangjiakou City, Hebei Province.</li>
        <li>Mandatory consumer-protection rights in the Customer’s jurisdiction are not affected.</li>
      </ul>

